    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d979">

                <pb facs="0764" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/7645</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"> Pacific Mail Steamship Company to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Francisco</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 30, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your wire 29th. Our steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Newport</hi> ordered call
                    Manzanillo northbound; due there about third or fourth. Passenger certificate
                    only allows 68 cabin, 42 steerage. Number passengers on board not known. If
                    United States Government instructs collector of this port that no penalty or
                    fine will be inflicted on Pacific Mail Steamship Company or steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Newport</hi> if she brings on this voyage people in
                    excess of her certificates we will instruct Captain <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Newport</hi> to take all passengers he can accommodate at Mexican ports
                    otherwise many may be refused passage.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pacific Mail Steamship Company</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
